    {
      "value": "<p>The largest of the icy moons, resurfaced repeatedly by ammonia-water slush that erupts in sheets rather than from vents. The flows overlap across the trailing hemisphere in a mat several hundred metres thick. Nothing has been recovered alive from any of them, although fresh slush stays warm enough to support life for several years at a time.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
